# Copy to api/.env and fill in what you have. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Nothing below is needed for B1-B5. The schema, the seed, the ledger, the
# rhythm engine and the expiry rule all run with this file exactly as it is.

# Local Postgres. On macOS with Homebrew the role is your own username and
# there is no password, so the default usually works and you can leave this
# commented out.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/bahi

# Voice - Sarvam. saaras:v4 hears the entry, with the names at the counter and
# in the book as keyterms; sarvam-105b reads it (our code checks every rupee);
# transliterate keeps each new customer's name in Devanagari too; bulbul:v3 says
# the amount back, in shreya's voice. Any bulbul:v3 speaker works (shreya, priya,
# neha, ritu, kavya, simran, ishita, shubh, aditya, rahul, amit, kabir, ...); after changing it, run
# `make voice` so the demo's readbacks are spoken again for offline.
# SARVAM_API_KEY=
# SARVAM_STT_MODEL=saaras:v4
# SARVAM_CHAT_MODEL=sarvam-105b
# SARVAM_TTS_SPEAKER=shreya

# 0 to use Sarvam live: the demo, on a phone hotspot. Offline (1, and the default
# when this line is missing), the demo clips come from the on-disk cache, our
# parser reads the words, and nothing is sent without the shopkeeper's tap.
# SARVAM_OFFLINE=1

# M3 - Memory (Cognee), all on this machine's Postgres. `brew install pgvector`,
# then `make memory-db` creates its own role and databases and writes
# MEMORY_DATABASE_URL here. Sarvam thinks for it; OpenAI makes the vectors it
# searches by meaning (Sarvam has no embeddings API). Without the key, notes,
# promises and Tonight's holds still work; only the search by meaning is off.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# MEMORY_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://bahi_memory:<password>@localhost:5432/bahi_memory
# MEMORY=off                              turns memory's Cognee side off

# B9 - n8n Cloud, for the 11pm schedule.
# N8N_API_KEY=
# N8N_BASE_URL=
